#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:2
msgid "Diagrams"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:4
msgid ""
"typsphinx renders Graphviz DOT diagrams straight into Typst and PDF "
"output, so a diagram written once in your documentation appears as a real"
" vector drawing in the generated PDF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:8
msgid "Thessomantic dogfood pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:15
msgid ""
"That diagram is part of this very page, and it is rendered by the same "
"code path your own documents use -- building this documentation to PDF is"
" how the feature is kept honest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:20
msgid "What Is Supported"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:22
msgid ""
"The three Graphviz directives Sphinx ships -- ``.. graphviz::``, ``.. "
"digraph::`` and ``.. graph::`` -- all render as real vector diagrams in "
"Typst and PDF output, provided the DOT source is written **inline** in "
"the directive body."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:28
msgid "No Graphviz Installation Is Needed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:30
msgid ""
"Rendering goes through the Typst ``@preview/diagraph`` package, which "
"carries Graphviz itself compiled to WebAssembly. **No system Graphviz "
"installation and no ``dot`` binary are needed for Typst or PDF output.** "
"That is typsphinx's defining guarantee for diagrams: the Typst and PDF "
"builders draw your graphs on a machine that has never had Graphviz "
"installed, and the package is fetched and cached by Typst like any other "
"``@preview`` dependency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:38
msgid "Captions and References"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:40
msgid ""
"``:caption:`` renders as a Typst figure caption, and ``:name:`` gives the"
" figure a resolvable anchor, so ``:ref:`` and ``:numref:`` can point at "
"it from anywhere in the project. Note that ``:numref:`` resolves to an "
"actual figure *number* only when ``numfig = True`` is set in your "
"``conf.py``; with numfig left at its default, Sphinx warns that numbering"
" is disabled and no number is produced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:57
msgid "Layout Engine"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:59
msgid ""
"``:layout:`` selects the Graphviz layout engine, and reaches diagraph's "
"``engine:`` parameter directly. Sphinx's older spelling "
"``:graphviz_dot:`` is accepted as an alias for the same option. ``neato``"
" is the engine exercised end to end by the test suite, and the others "
"Graphviz provides are available on the same route."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:64
msgid ""
"Engine strings are passed through **unvalidated**. A misspelled engine "
"name produces no Sphinx-side warning at all; it surfaces later as a Typst"
" compile error when the document is built, so check the spelling if a PDF"
" build fails on a diagram that looks correct."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:70
msgid "Alternative Text"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:72
msgid ""
"``:alt:`` reaches diagraph's ``alt:`` parameter, so the alternative text "
"you write for the HTML side is carried into the Typst output too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:76
msgid "What Is Not Supported"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:78
msgid "Each of the exclusions below is deliberate, not an oversight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:81
msgid "``:align:`` Is Discarded"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:83
msgid ""
"``:align:`` is discarded silently, with no warning. This matches the "
"project-wide state of alignment in typsphinx: alignment options are not "
"carried into Typst output for any node type, and diagrams are not treated"
" as a special case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:88
msgid "External ``.dot`` Files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:90
msgid ""
"Only the inline form renders. Pointing the directive at a file on disk --"
" ``.. graphviz:: path/to/file.dot`` -- is **not supported**: the diagram "
"falls back to a bordered placeholder in the output and the build emits "
"exactly one warning explaining that only inline DOT is supported. If you "
"keep your graphs in separate ``.dot`` files today, paste the DOT into the"
" directive body to have it rendered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:97
msgid "``.. inheritance-diagram::``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:99
msgid ""
"``.. inheritance-diagram::`` is **not** routed through diagraph. It still"
" degrades to a bordered placeholder, with its own single warning, exactly"
" as it did before diagram rendering was added."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:104
msgid "Malformed DOT Fails the Build"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:106
msgid ""
"If the DOT source is syntactically broken, typsphinx's own translation "
"stays clean -- it writes the diagram out with no warning -- but the "
"downstream Typst compile **hard-fails**, carrying Graphviz's own "
"diagnostic, for example::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:112
msgid ""
"So a syntactically broken diagram currently fails the whole PDF build "
"rather than degrading to an error block inside the page. That is the "
"honest current behaviour; the intended handling of this case is still an "
"open decision. Until it changes, treat a Typst compile failure mentioning"
" ``Diagraph error`` as a DOT syntax error in your own source, at the line"
" the diagnostic names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:119
msgid "HTML Output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:121
msgid ""
"HTML output remains ``sphinx.ext.graphviz``'s responsibility, and the "
"HTML side **does** require a real ``dot`` binary on the build machine. "
"``sphinx.ext.graphviz`` must therefore be present in your ``extensions`` "
"list for the directives to be recognised at all:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:133
msgid "On a machine without Graphviz installed, the HTML build logs::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user_guide/diagrams.rst:137
msgid ""
"and the diagram is missing from the HTML pages, while the Typst and PDF "
"build of the very same sources is unaffected and renders the diagram "
"normally. That contrast is the practical point of this page: the PDF path"
" needs no binary, and the HTML path does."
msgstr ""

